 Council CA/D 10/22 of 13.10.2022 (OJ EPO 2022, A101), which entered into force on 01.11.2023. See notice from the EPO of 25.11.2022 concerning legal changes to support digital transformation in the patent grant procedure (OJ EPO 2022, A114) and of 06.03.2023 concerning amended Rules 126 EPC, Rule 127 EPC and Rule 131 EPC (OJ EPO 2023, A29).","If the European Patent Office establishes that the document was delivered to the addressee more than seven days after the date it bears, a period for which the deemed receipt of that document is the relevant event under Rule 131, paragraph 2, shall expire later by the number of days by which the seven days were exceeded."]},{"title":"Rule 126. Request for Admissions","url":"https://govt.westlaw.com/azrules/Document/ND71A3FD0427511EAB1B4B3B7F711605F?transitionType=Default","is_source_local":false,"is_source_both":false,"description":"<strong>Following each request there must be a space that is large enough for the party to whom it is sent to state whether the request is admitted or denied, or to provide an objection</strong>. Requests for admissions must include a notice that provides the specific calendar date that the responses are due ...","profile":{"name":"Westlaw","url":"https://govt.westlaw.com/azrules/Document/ND71A3FD0427511EAB1B4B3B7F711605F?transitionType=Default","long_name":"govt.westlaw.com","img":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/9dEYjlYB2EvHbagu5BBM7A21uha4bVsaIdONwYXfA_0/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMWZiZDZjYWU5/Y2UyMDZmMWI3M2Ji/NmZkYjJhMjI1MDVh/ZWY3OTU2MTk0NDky/NzgxMTM4ZTM4Y2Q1/ZWQ5NDk0OS9nb3Z0/Lndlc3RsYXcuY29t/Lw"},"language":"en","family_friendly":true,"type":"search_result","subtype":"generic","is_live":false,"meta_url":{"scheme":"https","netloc":"govt.westlaw.com","hostname":"govt.westlaw.com","favicon":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/9dEYjlYB2EvHbagu5BBM7A21uha4bVsaIdONwYXfA_0/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMWZiZDZjYWU5/Y2UyMDZmMWI3M2Ji/NmZkYjJhMjI1MDVh/ZWY3OTU2MTk0NDky/NzgxMTM4ZTM4Y2Q1/ZWQ5NDk0OS9nb3Z0/Lndlc3RsYXcuY29t/Lw","path":"› azrules  › Document  › ND71A3FD0427511EAB1B4B3B7F711605F"},"extra_snippets":["Any matter admitted under this rule is conclusively established in the pending lawsuit unless the court permits an admission to be withdrawn or amended. The court may permit an admission to be withdrawn or amended only when it serves the interests of justice and when it furthers a decision of the lawsuit on its merits.","If a party fails to admit the genuineness of a document or the truthfulness of a matter as provided in a request under this rule, and the requesting party thereafter proves at a hearing or at trial that a document is genuine or that a matter is true, the court may consider whether there was any reasonable basis for the denial, and if there is none, the court may impose a penalty under Rule 127(d) against the party who denied the request.","A request for admissions may concern any matter permitted under Rule 122(a).","Following each request there must be a space that is large enough for the party to whom it is sent to state whether the request is admitted or denied, or to provide an objection. Requests for admissions must include a notice that provides the specific calendar date that the responses are due based on these rules."]},{"title":"Rule 126: Search and Seizure Guidelines | PDF | Search And Seizure | Probable Cause","url":"https://www.scribd.com/document/265820163/Rule-126-Search-and-Seizure","is_source_local":false,"is_source_both":false,"description":"Rule 126 Search and Seizure - Free download as Word Doc (.doc / .docx), PDF File (.pdf), Text File (.txt) or read online for free. This document outlines the legal rules and requirements regarding search and seizure in the Philippines according to Rule 126 of the Rules of Court.","profile":{"name":"Scribd","url":"https://www.scribd.com/document/265820163/Rule-126-Search-and-Seizure","long_name":"scri