"is_source_both":false,"description":"Failure scenario: an author asks, ... under rule 51 it is a violation. | Keep rule 126 to one direction: <strong>a private source keeps nothing but the private assets</strong>....","profile":{"name":"GitHub","url":"https://github.com/Luolc/agent-constitution/pull/301","long_name":"github.com","img":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/xxsA4YxzaR0cl-DBsH9-lpv2gsif3KMYgM87p26bs_o/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvYWQyNWM1NjA5/ZjZmZjNlYzI2MDNk/N2VkNmJhYjE2MzZl/MDY5ZTMxMDUzZmY1/NmU3NWIzNWVmMjk0/NTBjMjJjZi9naXRo/dWIuY29tLw"},"language":"en","family_friendly":true,"type":"search_result","subtype":"generic","is_live":false,"meta_url":{"scheme":"https","netloc":"github.com","hostname":"github.com","favicon":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/xxsA4YxzaR0cl-DBsH9-lpv2gsif3KMYgM87p26bs_o/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvYWQyNWM1NjA5/ZjZmZjNlYzI2MDNk/N2VkNmJhYjE2MzZl/MDY5ZTMxMDUzZmY1/NmU3NWIzNWVmMjk0/NTBjMjJjZi9naXRo/dWIuY29tLw","path":"› Luolc  › agent-constitution  › pull  › 301"},"thumbnail":{"src":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/fHl4K8hEZjS4QD0MWrpSFiIrYH5pmKPYA6Gy4At0tkY/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cHM6Ly9vcGVu/Z3JhcGguZ2l0aHVi/YXNzZXRzLmNvbS9j/MTUzN2YzZmM3YjA5/ZTM2ZmMyYmRiNjdk/ZWJmYjFhOWZjNDE3/YjhmYzZmMDFmMTU3/OTkxMzRhNDhiYTll/YzA4L0x1b2xjL2Fn/ZW50LWNvbnN0aXR1/dGlvbi9wdWxsLzMw/MQ","original":"https://opengraph.githubassets.com/c1537f3fc7b09e36fc2bdb67debfb1a9fc417b8fc6f01f15799134a48ba9ec08/Luolc/agent-constitution/pull/301","logo":false},"extra_snippets":["Constitution, rule library and compiler for coding-agent instructions - Rule 126: a private source holds only private assets by Luolc · Pull Request #301 · Luolc/agent-constitution","The second half is already rule 51 (public-repo-no-private-details): a public source of rules is in a public repository, and rule 51 forbids a machine name, an account name, secret-store paths, a private repository name and agent names there. Rule 51 also says \"A principal's yes under {@rule:34} does not lift this rule\". Rule 126's \"without the principal's answer that allows it\" lifts it for exactly that case.","Failure scenario: an author asks, a principal says yes, and the author writes a host name into a public rule. Under rule 126 that complies; under rule 51 it is a violation. | Keep rule 126 to one direction: a private source keeps nothing but the private assets.","Rule 51 read in full at this head (rules/51.toml, verification): its list of what may not be written to a public repository, and the sentence that a principal's yes does not lift it. Checked and fine: id = 126 and the file name match. The authority pair does not include one provision under the other (rule 104)."]},{"title":"Elementary Cellular Automaton, Rule 126 - Nikos Papadopoulos","url":"https://www.4rknova.com/blog/2019/03/18/elementary-cell-auto-rule-126","is_source_local":false,"is_source_both":false,"description":"<strong>A rule borrows its unique name by its numerical byte value</strong>. Each bit encodes the final state of the transitioning cell depending on a specific input state. That input state is defined by the index of the bit encoded in binary.","page_age":"2019-03-18T00:00:00","profile":{"name":"4rknova","url":"https://www.4rknova.com/blog/2019/03/18/elementary-cell-auto-rule-126","long_name":"4rknova.com","img":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/yyg97J-IlFM_n_fRGgCbstPLmqlF_plDuvQcf2BK2KI/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMjhmNDE4OWU3/NTNhNmY0NTFjYzc0/OTAzN2JlYzIyYzJi/NWE3NmFkZDEwMTM0/ZWM1MWJmNzRiOWZi/ZmNiOWMwNy93d3cu/NHJrbm92YS5jb20v"},"language":"en","family_friendly":true,"type":"search_result","subtype":"generic","is_live":false,"meta_url":{"scheme":"https","netloc":"4rknova.com","hostname":"www.4rknova.com","favicon":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/yyg97J-IlFM_n_fRGgCbstPLmqlF_plDuvQcf2BK2KI/rs:fit:32:32:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL2Zhdmlj/b25zLnNlYXJjaC5i/cmF2ZS5jb20vaWNv/bnMvMjhmNDE4OWU3/NTNhNmY0NTFjYzc0/OTAzN2JlYzIyYzJi/NWE3NmFkZDEwMTM0/ZWM1MWJmNzRiOWZi/ZmNiOWMwNy93d3cu/NHJrbm92YS5jb20v","path":"› blog  › 2019  › 03  › 18  › elementary-cell-auto-rule-126"},"thumbnail":{"src":"https://imgs.search.brave.com/QfjghsjsawVPikmhuxGGSDcuVnFaSycl24BIlkHPpI0/rs:fit:200:200:1:0/g:ce/aHR0cDovL3d3dy40/cmtub3ZhLmNvbS9h/c3NldHMvaW1nL3Bv/c3RzL2VsZW1lbnRh/cnlfY2VsbF9hdXRv/X3J1bGVfMTI2L29n/LXdpZGUucG5n","original":"http://www.4rknova.com/assets/img/posts/elementary_cell_auto_rule_126/og-wide.png","logo":false},"age":"March 18, 2019","extra_snippets":["111 110 101 100 011 010 001 000 126 = 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0 in binary · Below is sample code for rule 126, implemented in a GLSL fragment shader.","Putting all this together, rule 126 is illustrated below:","To visualize it in 2D we // choose time as our second dimension. Each successive // line in the grid is the evolution of the previous // population in the line above. if (gc.y - .5 == t) { bool pl = S(gc, vec2(-1,1)) , pc = S(gc, vec2( 0,1)) , pr = S(gc, vec2( 1,1)); // Rule 126.","A rule borrows its unique name by its numerical byte value. Each bit encodes the final state of the transitioning cell depending on a specific input state. That input state is defined by the index of the bit encoded in binary. As the maximum index has a value of 7, we need 3 bits to encode that value."]},{"title":"According to Rule 126, Sections 7 and 8 of the Rules of Court ...","url":"https://www.facebook.com/tribunephl/posts/according-to-rule-126-sections-7-and-8-of-the-rules-of-court-government-agents-m/999290892247331/","is_source_local":false,"is_source_both":false,"description":"Daily Tribune. 2,417,937 likes · 2,517,940 talking about this. The hottest news in politics, business, sports, lifestyle and entertainment is on Daily Tribune.","profile":{"name":"Facebook","url":"https://www.facebook.com/tribunephl/posts/according-to-rule-126-sections-7-and-8-of-the-rules-of-court-government-agents-m/999290892247331/","l